    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42739" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sătŭrĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, m.
		satur. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of a lost comedy of Plautus</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 3, 3,
				14</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The name of a parasite in the Persa of Plautus;</i>
			hence, in a lusus verbb.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Essurio venio, non advenio saturio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 1, 3, 23</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
